+
+  // Lobium: farble the observer's rects with the SAME kernel, seed and policy that farble
+  // Element::GetBoundingClientRect.
+  //
+  // To a page, entry.boundingClientRect IS getBoundingClientRect() - the spec defines it that way -
+  // but IntersectionObserver computes it from layout instead of calling that method, so it bypassed
+  // the client-rect hook entirely. One observer callback next to one getBoundingClientRect() call
+  // therefore returned two different numbers for the same box, which is a contradiction no honest
